Package: treeshapesim
Title: Simulate Trees with Separately Controlled Imbalance and Branching
    Times
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Diogo B.", "Provete", , "dbprovete@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates rooted, binary, ultrametric trees in which
    topological imbalance and the distribution of branching times are set
    by separate parameters. The topology is drawn from Aldous'
    beta-splitting model and the internode intervals from a pure-birth
    process in which each of k lineages splits at rate k^c. Because the
    gamma statistic depends only on the internode intervals and the
    Colless index only on the topology, beta mainly controls imbalance and
    c mainly controls gamma.
